From: Diego Nepomuceno Marcos <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:36:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] =?UTF-8?q?Cloud-Dialer:=20proper=20call=20filtering?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20screened-call=20history,=20per-number=20allowlis?=
 =?UTF-8?q?t,=20spam=20categories,=20expanded=20offline=20spam=20DB?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ScreeningLog (pure JVM model) + ScreeningLogStore: every silently rejected
  call (blocked number, spam rule, not-in-contacts, hidden) is recorded with
  a reason code to a private capped JSON file — no more calls vanishing
  without a trace in contacts_only mode.
- ScreeningLogActivity: newest-first history with per-entry actions —
  call back, always-allow, block, copy. Clear-history menu.
- Per-number allowlist (Config.allowedNumbers): allowed numbers ALWAYS ring,
  overriding every screening rule; managed from the history and
  Settings > Call screening > Allowed numbers.
- SpamMatcher.match() exposes the matched rule/category (reason codes,
  in-call warning).
- spam_patterns.json v2: broader conservative premium-rate/scam coverage
  (US 900/976, UK 09x/070, DE 0900/0137, FR 089x, ES 80x/905/907, IT
  899/144/166, +882-13 satellite, +8809/+889/+37256).
- JVM testers: ScreeningLogTest (roundtrip, cap, fail-open parse) +
  SpamMatcherTest category assertion.
